It is only eleven o'clock, but it is already really hot in the office.
Jonas, Nele and I are standing in the kitchen taking a break.
"Do we want to barbecue in the park this evening?" Jonas asks us.
I think the idea is great, because today is the warmest day so far.
"Have you already planned anything?" I ask the two of them.
"Yes, who has organized what?" asks Nele.
"I brought my small grill this morning," Jonas says proudly.
"And I already bought charcoal yesterday," says Nele.
"But we don't have any food or drinks yet," says Jonas.
"I am going quickly to the supermarket during the lunch break," I suggest.
"I will buy a few snacks and something to drink."
"Are you already buying meat for the grill too?" Nele asks me.
"No, that is not a good idea," I answer.
"It is much too hot in the office today."
"The meat will go bad quickly here because our fridge is too small."
"True, the fridge was already completely full yesterday," says Jonas.
"Then we will buy the meat later together on the way to the park."
I nod, because that is a very good plan.
I am already really looking forward to the evening.
